1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:05,811
This is the Aedes aegypti, it transmits the Dengue virus.

2
00:00:05,811 --> 00:00:10,046
The Aedes albopictus, better known as the tiger mosquito

3
00:00:10,046 --> 00:00:12,239
can also transmit this virus.

4
00:00:12,239 --> 00:00:15,719
Female Aedes lay their eggs in standing water.

5
00:00:15,719 --> 00:00:20,484
An egg takes between 7 and 10 days to become an adult mosquito.

6
00:00:21,984 --> 00:00:26,894
Without any control measures, dengue spreads through mosquito bites.

7
00:00:26,894 --> 00:00:28,627
Only females bite humans

8
00:00:28,627 --> 00:00:31,876
as they need blood for their eggs to develop.

9
00:00:31,876 --> 00:00:36,498
Dengue symptoms include high fever, intense headache, body aches

10
00:00:36,498 --> 00:00:38,375
and red spots on the skin.

11
00:00:39,876 --> 00:00:44,119
With individual measures, such as repellent, long clothing

12
00:00:44,119 --> 00:00:48,070
and mosquito nets, some people can protect themselves.

13
00:00:48,070 --> 00:00:50,412
But other measures can help too.

14
00:00:51,912 --> 00:00:54,877
Collective measures make a big difference!

15
00:00:54,877 --> 00:00:57,772
Vaccines protect people even when bitten.

16
00:00:57,772 --> 00:01:00,879
Insecticides reduce the mosquito population.

17
00:01:00,879 --> 00:01:06,528
The combination of different measures strengthens the fight against the disease.

18
00:01:08,028 --> 00:01:11,213
When we take care of the environment, removing trash

19
00:01:11,213 --> 00:01:14,706
covering water containers, and eliminating breeding sites

20
00:01:14,706 --> 00:01:20,772
mosquitoes lose their breeding grounds and have no place to lay their eggs and develop into adults!

21
00:01:22,272 --> 00:01:25,400
The environment makes all the difference.

22
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:29,367
Rain and trash together produce more breeding sites.

23
00:01:29,367 --> 00:01:31,885
Cleaning and care eliminate them.

24
00:01:31,885 --> 00:01:35,471
In dense urban areas, the risk is even greater.

25
00:01:36,972 --> 00:01:43,830
Dengue has 4 different serotypes and the same mosquitoes that transmit Zika and chikungunya.

26
00:01:43,830 --> 00:01:48,676
But with knowledge and collective action, we can win this battle.

27
00:01:48,676 --> 00:01:49,943
Protect yourself.

28
00:01:49,943 --> 00:01:51,658
Protect your community.

29
00:01:51,658 --> 00:01:53,820
Take care of the environment.
